==== Opening the case ====

Opening the case is pretty straight-forward, but it will require a T-8 Torx screwdriver.

  - Set the case on a flat surface, bottom down.
  - Around the rim of the lid of the case there are 12x T-8 Torx screws. Remove them.
  - Gently lift the lid of the case off and set it to the side.
  - ???
  - PROFIT!

To reassemble the device, please follow the disassembly instructions in reverse.
==== Serial ====
-> [[docs:techref:hardware:port.serial]] general information about the serial port, serial port cable, etc.

== External Port (RJ-45) ==

This router has a traditional serial console port exposed via an RJ-45 connector on the front of the unit. This console port is for entering failsafe or debugging modes in early boot. Once booted, it functions as a standard tty with login capabilities. In the retail packaging of this device, an RJ-45 -> DB-9 cable is provided.

== Internal Port ==

Internally there is an exposed 4 pin header that functions as a 3.3V serial port for the bootloader, U-Boot. Here you can do everything you'd expect from a first stage bootloader, including debrick capabilities.\\
Looking from the front of the router (switch ports facing you), the layout of the internal port is as follows:\\

|V+|GND|TX|RX|

^ Serial connection parameters\\ for TRENDnet TEW-829DRU  | 115200, 8N1 (External and Internal) |

==== JTAG ====
JTAG functionality exists according to tools supplied in OEM support bundle. Further research required to discover test-points.


